SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE

Multi-panel scientific workflow/data figure showing a CellWhisperer interface applied to the Tabula Sapiens dataset. Panels include:  
a) browser-style interface with a score histogram, UMAP-like cell embedding, chat protocol area, and instructions for text query, score-based selection, visual selection, and natural-language chat;  
b) large UMAP scatter plot colored by CellWhisperer score for the query “structural cells with immune functions,” with dashed annotations for macrophages, endothelium, epithelial, stromal, pericyte-like, and selected fibroblast-like regions;  
c) chat transcript where the user asks about selected cells and immune-function relevance, with CellWhisperer responses mentioning fibroblasts, extracellular matrix remodeling, interferon/immune genes, and pathways;  
d) UMAP showing mean expression of genes mentioned by CellWhisperer, with a log-scale expression color legend and selected cell cluster circled.

The main visible finding is that natural-language querying highlights specific cell populations, including selected fibroblast-like cells, and links them to immune-related gene expression patterns in the embedding.

